  // the block cursor (fish-autosuggestion style: `$ ▊try 'ls' ⏎`) to signal
  // "this is alive". One-shot per page view — any interaction before the timer
  // fires cancels it, any after dismisses it, and it never re-arms. Under
  // prefers-reduced-motion the full text appears statically (no typing).
  const HINT_TEXT = "try 'ls' ⏎";
  const HINT_DELAY_MS = 4000;
  const HINT_TYPE_MS = 70; // per-character typing cadence

  // Navigation beat (change cuur): cd/open/install no longer navigate on the
  // same tick as Enter — instant navigation off a playful exploration surface
  // reads as a misclick, yanking the visitor away before the `opening …` line
  // even registers. Instead the handler prints where it's headed (a real
  // clickable link) and navigates after this beat; Ctrl-C cancels the pending
  // timer (see navigateWithBeat / the Ctrl-C branch in onKeydown).
  const NAV_BEAT_MS = 900;

  // On-screen command bar (change by18): the chip roster, in display order.
  // Touch users get one-tap access to the commands the ghost hint and `help`
